mode: "100644"
text: "# AGYOS path to completion\n\nThis checklist is local. Git tracks TOON document sources, and CI rejects tracked Markdown. Work on `main` using the repository's commit identity. Run tests, builds, dependency resolution, lint, packaging, and renders in GitHub Actions. Use `uv` for Python and Obscura headless for browser checks.\n\n## Current evidence\n\n- [x] GitHub Actions verified **6,353 TOON records** against the original Git blobs and file modes. [Conversion evidence](https://github.com/krishujeniya/AGYOS/actions/runs/44517089138)\n- [x] `main` at `85f506742f781e9f76587faa7a2674fef2c2ac92` tracks **zero Markdown files** and **6,353 Markdown-derived TOON sources**. The installer generates compatibility files for native AGY discovery.\n- [x] Validation, Pages, the documentation image, and the existing Council suite passed. The overall cutover CI failed because secret detection flagged ten matches across six documents. [Cutover CI](https://github.com/krishujeniya/AGYOS/actions/runs/44517491844)\n- [x] Security Toolkits passed for the cutover revision. [Security Toolkits](https://github.com/krishujeniya/AGYOS/actions/runs/44517491919)\n- [ ] Record the final conclusion of the Video Toolkits run, which was in progress when this checklist was written. [Video Toolkits](https://github.com/krishujeniya/AGYOS/actions/runs/44517491722)\n\n## 1. Close the TOON cutover\n\n- [ ] Review and land the four working-tree fixes for upstream adapter headers, reinstallation after local edits, plugin rules generated from TOON, and installer regressions.\n- [ ] Compare each redacted scanner finding with the decoded document and its pre-conversion Git blob. Record the path, rule, and disposition without printing credential values. Remove any real credential from active sources and coordinate revocation with the owner. For confirmed examples or format false positives, use unmistakable placeholders or preserve the instructions in a representation the scanner interprets correctly. Keep secret detection and its negative control active. Close each original finding even if a later incremental scan passes.\n- [ ] Verify installation in CI from a clean checkout and an existing workspace. Cover idempotent reruns, local edits, conflicting updates, the `GEMINI.md` symlink, executable modes, archived records, and skill discovery. Verify archived material stays outside the installed prompt set.\n- [ ] Strictly decode the tracked catalog and compare generated manifests with canonical TOON bodies. Require zero tracked Markdown after packaging and generation. Verify Pages and the documentation image from clean checkouts.\n- [ ] Record the publishing change. The rendered docs are supplied by Pages. The repository's native GitHub Markdown README, security policy, and PR templates require their original tracked filenames.\n\n## 2. Make Council use AGY CLI\n\n- [ ] Confirm AGY's supported headless command, response format, and isolation controls. Keep agent execution unavailable where the required read-only boundary cannot be enforced.\n- [ ] Replace the Claude, Codex, and Gemini CLI adapters in `scripts/council/src/adapters.ts` with AGY-backed reviewer roles. Give reviewers independent starting context. Have the chair record recommendations, disagreement, evidence, unresolved questions, and the verification checklist. Preserve historical session readability.\n- [ ] Serialize Council prompts as TOON. Keep trusted instructions, the user's question, and untrusted evidence distinct. Verify multiline input, missing AGY, permission denial, timeouts, and malformed responses.\n- [ ] Route substantive decisions and verification planning through Council by default. Keep approval gates, independent review, and CI evidence in place. A Council recommendation records advice.\n- [ ] Update Council skills, plugin rules, bootstrap messages, and CLI help. Exercise deliberation, listing, replay, revisit, and outcome recording. Use a recording AGY fixture in CI and track authenticated runtime verification separately.\n\n## 3. Remove unused alternate-host code\n\n- [ ] Trace callers from `bin/`, `mcp/`, AGY hooks, plugins, packaging, and CI before removing alternate-host executables, adapters, installer targets, or bridges. Claw has already been removed.\n- [ ] Remove the unused host-specific files. Preserve shared services still needed by AGY or CI. Check that a clean installation, skill routing, MCP, Council, and verification work without invoking another agent CLI. Add coverage for unsupported host selections where affected.\n\n## 4. Verify TOON delivery beyond skill manifests\n\n- [ ] Inventory Council, rules, agents, workflows, MCP, and prompt/cache commands. Identify direct TOON delivery and native AGY compatibility views, including linked reference data.\n- [ ] Migrate remaining active legacy prompt compilers while preserving transport schemas and requested response formats. Capture outgoing content at AGYOS-controlled boundaries in CI and independently decode it. Verify tasks, constraints, evidence, and output contracts. Cover stale caches and malformed data. Mark AGY-owned runtime behavior separately.\n- [ ] Audit Python invocations in touched paths and workflows against the `uv` rule. Resolve and verify dependency locks through GitHub Actions.\n\n## 5. Close on a single verified revision\n\n- [ ] Run `git diff --check`, confirm the staged scope, and verify the GitHub identity and branch. Commit and push the reviewed changes to `origin/main` under the repository's release rules.\n- [ ] Follow every applicable Actions workflow to completion for the **same final commit SHA**. Diagnose failures and verify the corrected revision. Record skipped and unavailable checks explicitly.\n- [ ] Obtain independent review. Record the commit SHA, Actions links, final document and skill counts, disposition of the ten scanner findings, and evidence from a clean AGY installation and Council decision.\n"
